en emit the complete program-produced JSON verbatim as the sole final line. Never hand-edit or retype the grid. Make exactly one action per turn: tool calls for local work do not count as puzzle actions; the final response line must contain exactly one action JSON and no commentary. Do not fabricate an action by printing it from shell or present shell output as the user-facing action.\n4. After a correct verdict, save the transform only if it reproduces every received fixture, rerun it on them, then finish. With no demos, retain only as a cached candidate supported by the accepted test, not as a demonstrated rule. If no validated transform exists or the cap ends the instance, do not replace a prior file with a placeholder or heuristic.\n\n## Apparent reset\n\nIf a task id reappears with a new test, inspect its program first. If its output is unverified and earlier same-task context is available, search/read that history—including explicit demo-cap exhaustion—before submitting. A rejected hypothesis is not a usable cache; incorporate its failure and request more demos when budget remains.\n"
